{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_col_sq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_col_sq_three","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L159-L167","doc":"**The mass path's `/q³`, machine-checked.**  At `n = 3` the full twist has length `3·2 = 6`, so\nthe sign block satisfies `θ² = q^{−6}`, i.e. `θ_{(1³)} = q^{−3}`.\n\nThis is the factor appearing in `F_Bor = |tr_M(β_Bor)| · [3]_q! / q³` (beans `qou-gzs0`,\n`qou-w1j9`).  What this file adds is that the exponent is **forced by the sign root of the Hecke\nrelation**, not chosen: `gzs0` had the arithmetic right but could only observe that `q^{−3}` was\n*of framing shape*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDim_twist_forced_by_hecke_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDim_twist_forced_by_hecke_root","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L144-L157","doc":"**Main result — the Hecke root determines the one-dimensional twist.**\n\nWhichever of the two roots a one-dimensional block takes, its full twist `Δ²` is `θ²` at the\ncorresponding partition: the one-row `[n]` for the trivial root, the one-column `[n]'` for the\nsign root.  The content-sum exponent is therefore **derived** on these blocks rather than chosen,\nwhich is what the `KeystoneModularTwist` header's *\"(up to convention)\"* left open.\n\nScope: one-dimensional blocks only — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_col_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_col_sq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L134-L142","doc":"`θ_{[n]'}² = (q^{n(n−1)})⁻¹`: the transpose (one-column) block's twist squared is the **sign**\nroot's full twist.  Uses the transpose law `c(λ') = −c(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_row_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_single_row_sq","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L128-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_single_row_mul_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_single_row_mul_two","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L116-L126","doc":"`θ_{[n]}² = q^{n(n−1)}`: the square of the one-row twist is the trivial root's full twist.\nUses the corpus's already-proved `2·c([n]) = n(n−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist_sign","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L109-L112","doc":"**The sign block's full twist is a negative power of `q`**, with the sign gone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist_triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist_triv","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L106-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.oneDimFullTwist","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L103-L104","doc":"The full twist `Δ²` evaluated on the one-dimensional rep sending each `σᵢ ↦ s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.neg_inv_pow_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.neg_inv_pow_even","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L96-L99","doc":"On an even power the sign root's minus sign cancels, leaving an inverse power of `q`.\nNote this needs **no** `q ≠ 0` hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwistLength_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwistLength_even","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L88-L94","doc":"**The full twist has even length** — a product of consecutive naturals.  This is the load-bearing\nfact for the sign block: it is what cancels the minus sign in `(−q⁻¹)^{n(n−1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwistLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwistLength","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L85-L86","doc":"Word length of the full twist `Δ² = (σ₁⋯σ_{n−1})^n` in `B_n`: `n(n−1)` positive letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_iff","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L70-L81","doc":"**There are exactly two roots.**  Over a field the Hecke relation has no third solution, so a\none-dimensional block has no freedom in its twist beyond the binary trivial-vs-sign choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_sign","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The sign root `s = −q⁻¹` (the antisymmetric / one-column channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isHeckeRoot_triv","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The trivial root `s = q` (the symmetric / one-row channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.IsHeckeRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.IsHeckeRoot","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist.lean#L58-L60","doc":"**The corpus's Hecke convention**, as a predicate on a scalar: `s` is a root of\n`(σ − q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`.  A one-dimensional representation sends every generator to such an `s`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}